#!/bin/bash
# fly-help — short Fly Lite tips and custom commands (flavor-aware).
set -euo pipefail

flavor=""
[[ -f /etc/fly-debian/stack-flavor ]] && flavor=$(tr -d '[:space:]' </etc/fly-debian/stack-flavor)

cat <<'EOF'
Fly-bian / Fly Lite 2.1 — help
==============================

First boot
----------
1. On the FLY-SETUP FAT volume, edit fly-start.txt (Wi-Fi, root, user).
2. Boot the board; wait for resize + Wi-Fi (several minutes).
3. SSH in:  ssh USER@BOARD_IP
4. Run:     fly-help      (this text)
EOF

if [[ $flavor == kiauh ]]; then
	cat <<'EOF'
            fly-kiauh     (KIAUH / cameras menu)

KIAUH image
-----------
Trees are pre-baked under /opt/fly-kiauh and copied into your home on first
user bind. There is no Simple-AF install script, fly-start menu, or Plymouth
boot splash.

  fly-kiauh
  # or:  ~/kiauh/kiauh.sh
  # cameras:  fly-kiauh cameras
  #        or fly-crowsnest-add-cams

Use KIAUH for printer.cfg and enabling services. Skip Moonraker "speedups" /
uvloop compile on this 512 MB board. Do not install Simple-AF (pellcorp).
KlipperScreen is optional but fragile (apt/X can OOM and break dpkg).
If it fails: sudo dpkg --configure -a && sudo apt -f install, then
fly-klipperscreen-prep (if present) before retrying. Prefer the
OctoEverywhere companion app over installing OctoEverywhere on this board.

512 MB OOM tips: free -h; dmesg | grep -i oom; confirm /swapfile via
swapon --show; install one package at a time; stop crowsnest during heavy
apt. Full guide: docs/boards/fly-lite-2.1/oom.md (Fly-bian repo).

Community extensions — avoid on 512 MB: OctoEverywhere, OctoApp, Obico,
OctoPrint, Spoolman (Docker), DroidKlipp. Caution: Mobileraker, Telegram
Bot, Moongate. Usually OK: SimplyPrint, KAMP, TMC Autotune, themes,
PrettyGCode, Klipper-Backup. See docs/kiauh-fly-lite.md.

Hardware notes
--------------
Soft reboot often hangs — use a 5 V power cycle.
Space power cycles / hard resets a few minutes apart. Cycling too quickly
or too often often leads to hung boots or kernel oops.

Web UIs (after services are up)
-------------------------------
  Fluidd    http://BOARD_IP/
  Mainsail  http://BOARD_IP:4409
  Camera    http://BOARD_IP/webcam/?action=stream

Custom commands (this image)
----------------------------
  fly-help
      This help text.

  fly-kiauh
      Menu: Start KIAUH / Add USB cameras.
      Direct: fly-kiauh cameras

  fly-crowsnest-add-cams [--dry-run]
      Find USB cameras under /dev/v4l/by-id and append [cam …] sections
      to ~/printer_data/config/crowsnest.conf, then restart Crowsnest.
      Skips the H3 cedrus encoder (/dev/video0).

  fly-moonraker-polkit [user]
      Install Moonraker PolKit rules + set enable_packagekit: False
      (clears Mainsail PolKit / PackageKit warnings on 512 MB).

  fly-klipperscreen-prep
      Recover dpkg and install KlipperScreen apt deps one package at a
      time (512 MB). Run before KIAUH → Install → KlipperScreen.

  fly-crowsnest-strip-placeholders
      Remove stock [cam web] / /dev/video0 placeholders from a conf file.

fly-start.txt (KIAUH)
---------------------
  Wi-Fi / locale / root / user only. No INSTALL_CMD, AUTO_CAMERAS,
  INSTALL_BOOT_DISPLAY, or GrumpyScreen keys on this image.

Image identity
--------------
  /etc/fly-debian/flybian-version
  /etc/fly-debian/flybian-image     e.g. Fly-bian-0.6_Fly-Lite-2.1_KIAUH-v6.0.0
  /etc/fly-debian/stack-rev
  /etc/fly-debian/stack-flavor      kiauh

Config file
-----------
  /boot/fly-start.txt   (FLY-SETUP FAT volume)

Serial: 115200 8N1, Type-C. Do not pulse DTR/RTS.
EOF
	exit 0
fi

cat <<'EOF'
            fly-start     (guided Simple-AF install / update)

Simple-AF (Simple-AF image)
---------------------------
Trees are pre-baked under /opt and copied into your home on first user bind.
Finish printer/probe with either:

  fly-start
  # or manually:
  ~/pellcorp/installer.sh --install --printer <printer> --probe <probe> [--mount <mount>]

Example:
  ~/pellcorp/installer.sh --install --printer creality-k1m-2023 --probe bltouch --mount Default

Update an existing install:
  ~/pellcorp/installer.sh --update
  # or choose "Update Simple AF" in fly-start

Do not install KIAUH on a Simple-AF card (or Simple-AF on a KIAUH card).
Do not install KlipperScreen on this 512 MB board — use GrumpyScreen.

512 MB OOM tips: free -h; dmesg | grep -i oom; swapon --show; after a
crash: sudo dpkg --configure -a && sudo apt -f install. Full guide:
docs/boards/fly-lite-2.1/oom.md (Fly-bian repo / GitHub).

Community / Moonraker add-ons — avoid on 512 MB: OctoEverywhere, OctoApp,
Obico, OctoPrint, Spoolman (Docker), KlipperScreen. Caution: Mobileraker,
Telegram Bot, Moongate. Usually OK: SimplyPrint, KAMP, TMC Autotune,
themes, PrettyGCode, Klipper-Backup. Prefer the OctoEverywhere companion
app over installing OctoEverywhere on this board.

Hardware notes
--------------
Soft reboot often hangs — use a 5 V power cycle.
Space power cycles / hard resets a few minutes apart. Cycling too quickly
or too often often leads to hung boots or kernel oops.

Web UIs (after install)
-----------------------
  Fluidd    http://BOARD_IP/
  Mainsail  http://BOARD_IP:4409
  Camera    http://BOARD_IP/webcam/?action=stream

Custom commands (this image)
----------------------------
  fly-help
      This help text.

  fly-moonraker-polkit [user]
      Install Moonraker PolKit rules + set enable_packagekit: False
      (clears Mainsail PolKit / PackageKit warnings on 512 MB).

  fly-start
      Interactive menu driven by fly-start.txt on FLY-SETUP /boot:
        1) Run Full Install Script  — INSTALL_CMD, then optional:
             AUTO_CAMERAS, ENABLE_GRUMPYSCREEN, INSTALL_BOOT_DISPLAY,
             GRUMPY_DISPLAY_ROTATE
        2) Update Simple AF         — ~/pellcorp/installer.sh --update
        3) Enable boot display      — Plymouth Simple-AF splash
        4) Disable boot display     — text boot sequence (diagnostics)
        5) Show GrumpyScreen rotation
        6) Set GrumpyScreen rotation (0°/90°/180°/270°)
        7) Cancel

  fly-boot-display enable|disable|status
      Toggle the early-boot Plymouth splash without re-running install.
      disable → bootlogo=false (splash=verbose) so HDMI shows startup text.
      enable  → install/activate Simple-AF theme + bootlogo=true.
      Reboot after enable/disable. Same as fly-start menu 3 / 4.

  fly-crowsnest-add-cams [--dry-run]
      Find USB cameras under /dev/v4l/by-id and append [cam …] sections
      to ~/printer_data/config/crowsnest.conf, then restart Crowsnest.
      Skips the H3 cedrus encoder (/dev/video0).

  fly-grumpy-rotate [0|1|2|3]
      Set GrumpyScreen display_rotate in
      ~/printer_data/config/grumpyscreen.ini [ui] and restart the UI.
      Targets /dev/fb0 (Fly TFT V2 panel-mipi-dbi when fly-lite-tft is
      loaded; otherwise HDMI). Touch: Fly-LCD, Goodix Cap, or ADS7846.
      No argument: show current rotation + fb/touch. fly-start menu 5 / 6.

  fly-crowsnest-strip-placeholders
      Remove stock [cam web] / /dev/video0 placeholders from a conf file
      (used by the camera helper and image bake).

Display options in fly-start.txt
--------------------------------
  ENABLE_GRUMPYSCREEN=Yes|No
      Touch / status UI on the Fly-LCD after the OS is up (not a splash).

  INSTALL_BOOT_DISPLAY=Yes|No
      Plymouth early-boot logo (Simple-AF theme), same as:
      https://pellcorp.github.io/creality-wiki/rpi_boot_display/
      Simple-AF images bake plymouth + theme; this flag / fly-boot-display
      only enables or disables the splash (bootlogo=true|false).
      Toggle later with fly-boot-display / fly-start 3–4.

  GRUMPY_DISPLAY_ROTATE=0|1|2|3
      Writes display_rotate into ~/printer_data/config/grumpyscreen.ini
      [ui] after a full install (0°/90°/180°/270°). Leave blank to skip.
      Change later with fly-grumpy-rotate / fly-start 5–6.

Image identity
--------------
  /etc/fly-debian/flybian-version   e.g. 0.5
  /etc/fly-debian/flybian-image     e.g. Fly-bian-0.5_Fly-Lite-2.1_Simple-AF-58e5c1d
  /etc/fly-debian/stack-rev         e.g. 58e5c1d (Simple-AF) or KIAUH tag/SHA

Config file
-----------
  /boot/fly-start.txt   (FLY-SETUP FAT volume; also under first-boot/)
  Keys for fly-start: INSTALL_CMD, AUTO_CAMERAS,
  ENABLE_GRUMPYSCREEN, INSTALL_BOOT_DISPLAY, GRUMPY_DISPLAY_ROTATE

Serial: 115200 8N1, Type-C. Do not pulse DTR/RTS.
EOF
